When $bold(X)$ has multivariate density $f$ and distribution function $F$,
$
  f(x_1, ..., x_n) = (∂^n)/(∂ x_1 ... ∂ x_n) F(x_1, ..., x_n),
$
and probabilities of general regions are obtained by integration:
$
  PP((X_1, ..., X_n)^tp in B) = integral_B f(y_1, ..., y_n) dif y_1 ... dif y_n quad quad "for every" B subset.eq RR^n.
$
